  "title": "Media got fast, detailed, and repeatable",
  "summary": "April made Pollinations faster across every medium, easier to wire into tools and agents, and more capable for the steadily expanding garden of community apps.\n\nLTX-2, Sana, ACE-Step, and Nova Reel received major speed or capability upgrades, while 4K Wan models, gptimage-2, richer transcription, audio seeds, video seeds, and image reasoning modes gave builders more control over what comes back.\n\nThe SDK gained media, image-editing, device-auth, key-management, and reasoning support; the new Pollinations CLI brought the full stack to terminals; and MCP plus OpenClaw integrations made models, media, account tools, and coding agents easier to connect.\n\nGemini, Claude Opus 4.7, DeepSeek V4, Llama 3.3, Qwen, Kimi, MiniMax, and Qwen3-TTS joined or advanced in the registry, with routing work and edge execution keeping text and image requests responsive when upstreams became theatrical.\n\nThe showcase welcomed a broad crop of apps: native clients, games, creative tools, study aids, Android video pipelines, repository analyzers, bots, and terminal experiments. Regular health, attribution, and README updates kept the public map of that ecosystem usable.",
